# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/

# Any database, by glob rather than by name: production copies pulled down for diagnosis
# (prod_jobs.db and friends) are the ones most worth keeping out, and they are exactly the
# ones a named list never anticipates. Runs in journal_mode=wal, so -wal/-shm are the pair
# that actually appears; -journal is from rollback mode and never shows up.
#
# graphs.db is the one to keep out on privacy grounds rather than size: a LangGraph
# checkpoint stores the graph's whole state, and the profile graph's state holds the full
# text of every corpus document. That puts career history in a repo whose entire .gitignore
# policy exists to keep it out.
*.db
*.db.*
*.db.pre-*
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal

# The flock the pipeline stages serialize on. Always empty; the lock is the file, not
# its contents.
.pipeline.lock

# Credentials
.env

# Logging. logrotate writes app.log.1, app.log.2.gz and so on, and *.log matches only the
# .log suffix, so the rotated files need their own pattern.
*.log
*.log.[0-9]*

# Raw scrape payloads, archived for normalizer replay. Pruned to
# scraper.archive_retention_days on every non-dry run; ~300-400MB steady state.
raw_payloads/

# One-off probe results (scripts/probe_linkedin_page_wall.py). Raw measurement data,
# not something to commit -- findings belong in README.md/config.yaml comments once
# analyzed, not the jsonl itself.
experiments/

# Generated digests. Anchored to repo root: unanchored `digests/` also matched
# `careerradar/web/frontend-src/src/routes/digests/`, silently dropping that route from
# every commit.
/digests/

# Runtime state: rewritten on every sync and holds the PID lock. Tracked in the old repo by
# accident, which made every run show up as a dirty working tree.
sync_status.json

# The resume corpus. These are personal documents, and their source of truth is the separate
# `resume` repo -- this repo deliberately carries no career history. A fresh clone therefore
# has no corpus, and build_profile() warns loudly when it notices. Restore with
# scripts/sync_corpus.sh.
#
# Anchored to repo root: unanchored `resumes/` also matched
# `careerradar/web/frontend-src/src/routes/resumes/`, silently dropping that route from
# every commit.
/resumes/
achievements.md
current_resume.md

# Frontend build tooling. The Vite build output is generated by `npm run build` and served
# by FastAPI at runtime -- see `careerradar/web/app.py` -- not committed.
node_modules/
careerradar/web/frontend/dist/
